content.text:
The hold was loud with the rhythm of cranes, and you were ten, small enough to ride in the crook of a loader's arm. Everything aboard that freighter moved without a human hand: pallets sliding off to the dark, manifests rewritten as you watched. A foreman came down the gantry and told your mother the colony ships were not coming back, and she should stop asking after them. <npc>"Then I'll ask somewhere that will answer,"</npc> your mother said, and turned her back on the whole ledger-run, self-sorting hold. You have remembered that for years, and it still does not explain why she left.

