Tamsin Vey lifts her thumb from the ledger, and it stays closed anyway. "Fine," she says, flat as a receipt. "Hollow Spire is small. A friend here is worth more than a customer, and costs less to lose." She slides a stamped slip across the counter. It carries a berth number and a hour. <npc>"Come by when your credit's good, and bring the questions you'd rather not ask out loud."</npc> A loader grinds past, and she waits it out. <npc>"Who sent you my name?"</npc>

