The clerk stops at the end of your berth and holds the slate out without looking at it. "Hull Kobayashi IV," he reads, flat as a tariff. "Salvage flag was filed ahead of you. Someone wants you to know your wreck has been talked about." Behind him, two dockhands stop sorting crates and watch, and the amber berth lights flicker once more.

"Cutting through a hatch that's marked rigged gets noted," he says, still reading. <npc>"Station policy is that nobody breaches it, and anyone who tries answers to the dockmaster before the clamps release."</npc> He taps the slate and your hold on this berth goes to a countdown you can see from here, and he waits for you to say something.

